{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i am writing a detailed review of the movie \"the social network\" in all lower case as per your request.\n\n**movie title:** the social network\n**release year:** 2010\n**director:** david fincher\n**screenplay:** aaron sorkin\n**main cast:** jesse eisenberg, andrew garfield, joseph gordon-levitt, armie hammer\n\n**storyline:**\nthe movie the social network tells the story of the founding of facebook, a social networking site that started in a college dorm and became a global phenomenon. the film focuses on mark zuckerberg (jesse eisenberg), a harvard university student who creates a website called \"thefacebook\" with the help of his roommate eduardo saverin (andrew garfield). as the site gains popularity, mark's relationship with eduardo deteriorates, and he becomes embroiled in a lawsuit with the winn twins (armie hammer), who claim he stole their idea.\n\n**acting:**\n- jesse eisenberg delivers a stellar performance as mark zuckerberg, portraying him as a complex, slightly awkward, and intensely focused individual.\n- andrew garfield brings depth to eduardo saverin, making his character's downfall both poignant and understandable.\n- joseph gordon-levitt has a smaller but notable role as cameron wray, adding to the film's dynamic.\n- armie hammer convincingly plays the role of both cameron and tyler winn, highlighting the twins' sense of entitlement.\n\n**direction and cinematography:**\ndavid fincher's direction is impeccable, weaving together multiple timelines with ease. the cinematography is sleek, capturing the intensity of the characters' journeys and the rapid growth of facebook.\n\n**screenplay:**\naaron sorkin's screenplay is a masterpiece of dialogue-driven storytelling, making even the most tech-heavy conversations engaging and fast-paced.\n\n**music:**\ntrent reznor and atticus ross's soundtrack perfectly complements the film's mood, from the intense coding sequences to the more reflective moments.\n\n**critique:**\nwhile the movie is largely praised for its portrayal of events, some liberties were taken with the actual story of facebook's creation. however, these do not detract from the film's overall impact.\n\n**rating:** 4.5/5\n\n**recommendation:**\nthe social network is a must-watch for anyone interested in the intersection of technology, friendship, and ambition. it's a gripping tale that explores the highs and lows of success at a very young age.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -0.04083649069070816}, {"token": " am", "logprob": -1.3219144344329834}, {"token": " writing", "logprob": -0.036421991884708405}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.3522993326187134}, {"token": " detailed", "logprob": -0.04335487261414528}, {"token": " review", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -4.792098479811102e-05}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.012774069793522358}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.14804573357105255}, {"token": " all", "logprob": -0.0008382858941331506}, {"token": " lower", "logprob": -0.0024782679975032806}, {"token": " case", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.1002809926867485}, {"token": " per", "logprob": -0.693190336227417}, {"token": " your", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": " request", "logprob": -4.207999518257566e-05}, {"token": ".\n\n", "logprob": -0.1428397297859192}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.0028960451018065214}, {"token": "movie", "logprob": -0.00042000532266683877}, {"token": " title", "logprob": -0.05823533982038498}, {"token": ":**", "logprob": -0.0017303746426478028}, {"toke